CloudBurrow patch 7 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1116).

The bug: TO_JSON_STRING, TO_JSON and SAFE_TO_JSON wrote each value with
its own ToJSON, which does not follow GoogleSQL's JSON encodings table
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/json_functions#json_encodings).
A value reaches a function through SQLite, which has no BOOL, so a BOOL read
from a table (or built in a STRUCT) was written 1; a DATE, DATETIME, TIME or
TIMESTAMP was written without quotes, which is not JSON; a NUMERIC with a
fraction, and an INT64 or NUMERIC beyond 2^53, was not a string in
TO_JSON_STRING; +/-inf and NaN were +Inf, -Inf and NaN, not the strings
"Infinity", "-Infinity" and "NaN"; an INTERVAL was its canonical text, not
an ISO 8601 duration; a RANGE was its text, not {"start":...,"end":...};
TO_JSON kept a STRUCT's duplicate field names, and ignored
stringify_wide_numbers; and TO_JSON_STRING ignored pretty_print.

The patch has the formatter pass the first argument's static type to these
functions as one more argument (as CAST is passed its types), casts the
value to it as the row scanner casts a column, and encodes it by type
(internal/json_encoding.go). TO_JSON(NULL) and SAFE_TO_JSON(NULL) stay SQL
NULL, TO_JSON_STRING(NULL) stays "null", and GEOGRAPHY, which the table does
not list, is written as before. json_encoding_test.go fails without the
patch and passes with it.

